    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "how the campaign works",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Onboarding** (mmm/onboarding/PLAN.md). Server-driven emails E1\u2013E5 go through Brevo, one scheduled task per network and flow step, re-evaluated at send time. The live counters below explain campaign execution. The durable **email tracker** further counts distinct networks sent each flow step and their later behavior; it refreshes every 15 minutes and exports one bounded 28-day snapshot. `engaged` means click, landing click, attributed app open, connection, widget, feedback, or Pro start; an open alone is excluded because mailbox privacy prefetch can manufacture opens. E3 and E5 may share a template, so new events carry a separate exact `flow_step`; historical shared-template events are reported as `attribution_ambiguous`, never guessed. Detailed privacy-safe daily dimensions are available to the research loop at `GET /admin/onboarding/email-tracker`; raw network and message identifiers never enter Grafana or that endpoint. The nightly results rollup (02:00 UTC, `OnboardingResultsRollup`) remains the account-cohort experiment and retention source at `GET /admin/onboarding/results`."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "the funnel and the nightly results rollup",
